WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.867 --> 00:00:02.135
- Some of the people that serve

00:00:02.135 --> 00:00:03.436
with me on the House
of Representatives,

00:00:03.436 --> 00:00:06.940
even though they may
have noble intentions,

00:00:06.940 --> 00:00:10.243
they are useful fools
'cause what they think

00:00:10.243 --> 00:00:12.379 align:start size:94% position:6%
that what they're pedaling
is good for others.

00:00:12.379 --> 00:00:15.749 align:start size:88% position:13%
No, because they have
never had the experience

00:00:15.749 --> 00:00:18.385
of being or living
in Cuba or Venezuela.

00:00:18.385 --> 00:00:19.686
Go for two weeks to Havana.

00:00:19.686 --> 00:00:20.987 align:start size:81% position:19%
I always tell them
two weeks only,

00:00:20.987 --> 00:00:22.222
(Dave laughing)

00:00:22.222 --> 00:00:24.858
make it a week with
a Cuban family living

00:00:24.858 --> 00:00:28.495
with no dollars and waiting
to come to the United States.

00:00:28.495 --> 00:00:30.196
Go live with them for one week

00:00:30.196 --> 00:00:33.033
and then you tell me what
the beauties of socialism.

00:00:33.033 --> 00:00:36.503
Oh no, because we don't
really want the the Cuban

00:00:36.503 --> 00:00:39.272
or the Venezuelan type
of socialism really.

00:00:39.272 --> 00:00:40.907
So what socialism
would you like?

00:00:40.907 --> 00:00:41.908
- Right.

00:00:41.908 --> 00:00:44.477
(upbeat music)

00:00:48.681 --> 00:00:51.284
All right, day three of
three in DC continues.

00:00:51.284 --> 00:00:52.519
I'm still Dave Rubin.

00:00:52.519 --> 00:00:53.787 align:start size:81% position:19%
This is still "The
Rubin Report."

00:00:53.787 --> 00:00:54.954
And joining me today
is a congresswoman

00:00:54.954 --> 00:00:58.358 align:start size:84% position:16%
representing Florida's
27th District

00:00:58.358 --> 00:01:00.560
which happens to be my
district, Maria Salazar.

00:01:00.560 --> 00:01:01.494
(both quietly clapping)

00:01:01.494 --> 00:01:02.629
Welcome to "The Rubin Report."

00:01:02.629 --> 00:01:05.165 align:start size:88% position:13%
- Yes, good, and
welcome to District 27.

00:01:05.165 --> 00:01:06.099
- I can't promise you-

00:01:06.099 --> 00:01:07.500
- The ultimate melting pot.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:08.868
- Yeah, it is indeed.

00:01:08.868 --> 00:01:10.070
I can't promise you

00:01:10.070 --> 00:01:11.571 align:start size:88% position:13%
this is gonna be a very
combative interview

00:01:11.571 --> 00:01:15.208
because I told you when you
walked in I voted for you.

00:01:15.208 --> 00:01:16.976
Everyone in this
room voted for you.

00:01:16.976 --> 00:01:18.211
- Thank you, yes.

00:01:18.211 --> 00:01:19.712 align:start size:84% position:16%
Well, you know, you
guys are smart people.

00:01:19.712 --> 00:01:20.647
(Dave laughing)

00:01:20.647 --> 00:01:21.848
- And we're all pretty thrilled

00:01:21.848 --> 00:01:23.083 align:start size:81% position:19%
about what's going
on, obviously.

00:01:23.083 --> 00:01:24.084 align:start size:81% position:19%
- And now you live
in my district.

00:01:24.084 --> 00:01:25.718
- And I'm in your district.

00:01:25.718 --> 00:01:27.187
We're thrilled obviously

00:01:27.187 --> 00:01:29.122 align:start size:97% position:3%
with what's going on in
Florida, Miami specifically.

00:01:29.122 --> 00:01:30.590
- Yes.

00:01:30.590 --> 00:01:32.058 align:start size:97% position:3%
- So before we get into
the nuts and bolts of that,

00:01:32.058 --> 00:01:33.927 align:start size:97% position:3%
could you just give the
people that may not know you

00:01:33.927 --> 00:01:35.428
a little bit of your history?

00:01:35.428 --> 00:01:37.097
You have an interesting work
history and family history

00:01:37.097 --> 00:01:38.698
that I think frames a
lot of your politics.

00:01:38.698 --> 00:01:39.866
- Sure, of course.

00:01:39.866 --> 00:01:42.102 align:start size:84% position:16%
I was first generation
Cuban American.

00:01:42.102 --> 00:01:45.605
My parents came to
that city, 1960,

00:01:45.605 --> 00:01:48.208
thanks to the United States
that opened up the doors

00:01:48.208 --> 00:01:52.679
to 2 million Cubans who were
fleeing probably the most cruel

00:01:52.679 --> 00:01:55.882
and the most evil revolution
that the Americas has seen

00:01:55.882 --> 00:01:58.518
since the arrival of
Christopher Columbus.

00:01:58.518 --> 00:02:01.754 align:start size:84% position:16%
Completely, completely
a bad situation.

00:02:01.754 --> 00:02:03.723
So I grew up in Miami.

00:02:03.723 --> 00:02:07.894
I have an accent because my
parents could not find work,

00:02:07.894 --> 00:02:10.396 align:start size:84% position:16%
like many other
millions of Cubans,

00:02:10.396 --> 00:02:13.032 align:start size:84% position:16%
and we had to hop
from island to island.

00:02:13.032 --> 00:02:15.368
And I lived in Puerto
Rico some of the time,

00:02:15.368 --> 00:02:17.103
another time in Miami.

00:02:17.103 --> 00:02:18.471
That's why I speak Spanish.

00:02:18.471 --> 00:02:21.107
And I can communicate with 72%

00:02:21.107 --> 00:02:24.911 align:start size:97% position:3%
of my district that happens
to be Hispanic descent.

00:02:24.911 --> 00:02:26.946
- I may need you to help me
brush up on some Spanish-

00:02:26.946 --> 00:02:28.148
- Of course.

00:02:28.148 --> 00:02:29.415 align:start size:88% position:13%
- Because yes, everybody
down there is Cuban.

00:02:29.415 --> 00:02:31.217
- It's like, hey,
it's all Espanol.

00:02:31.217 --> 00:02:32.485
Yes, but we love-

00:02:32.485 --> 00:02:33.987
(both speaking in
foreign language)

00:02:33.987 --> 00:02:37.891
Yes, but we love the American
exceptionality, and I more,

00:02:37.891 --> 00:02:40.894 align:start size:88% position:13%
and that's why I
represent them proudly.

00:02:40.894 --> 00:02:42.562 align:start size:84% position:16%
I went to the
University of Miami.

00:02:42.562 --> 00:02:44.864
After that I started
working for Univision.

00:02:44.864 --> 00:02:47.167
I'm one of the founders
of Spanish television.

00:02:47.167 --> 00:02:48.134
- [Dave] Yeah.

00:02:48.134 --> 00:02:49.702
- Univision and Telemundo.

00:02:49.702 --> 00:02:53.239
Then I went to Harvard and
I worked hard at 35 years

00:02:53.239 --> 00:02:57.677 align:start size:84% position:16%
in front of the
camera paying my rent.

00:02:57.677 --> 00:03:01.181
And after that I decided to
come and serve the country.

00:03:01.181 --> 00:03:05.051
And believe me, this is a lot
harder and it pays a lot less.

00:03:05.051 --> 00:03:08.421 align:start size:97% position:3%
It is highly gratifying,
highly gratifying to be able

00:03:08.421 --> 00:03:11.224
to represent the American values

00:03:11.224 --> 00:03:12.692
in the United States Congress.

00:03:12.692 --> 00:03:14.227
- So my guys showed
me right before,

00:03:14.227 --> 00:03:16.496
your election history
is really interesting

00:03:16.496 --> 00:03:19.799
because in 2018 you
lost by three points.

00:03:19.799 --> 00:03:22.035 align:start size:84% position:16%
Then in 2020 you
won by three points.

00:03:22.035 --> 00:03:24.137
And then in 2022 you won by 13.

00:03:24.137 --> 00:03:25.371 align:start size:63% position:38%
- By 15.
- 15?

00:03:25.371 --> 00:03:27.407
I had 13 here, but
I'll go with 15.

00:03:27.407 --> 00:03:28.875
And that sort of is indicative-

00:03:28.875 --> 00:03:30.376
- In two years.

00:03:30.376 --> 00:03:31.511 align:start size:94% position:6%
- Of the direction that
Florida's going in, right?

00:03:31.511 --> 00:03:33.112
- Well, because the problem is

00:03:33.112 --> 00:03:37.517 align:start size:88% position:13%
that the word socialism,
it's highly scary.

00:03:37.517 --> 00:03:40.186
And every time a Democratic,

00:03:40.186 --> 00:03:43.323 align:start size:94% position:6%
a member of the
Democratic party mentions

00:03:43.323 --> 00:03:46.826
democratic socialism,
we run the other way.

00:03:46.826 --> 00:03:50.730
Whether you're registered as
Independent or as a Democrat,

00:03:50.730 --> 00:03:52.165
it doesn't matter.

00:03:52.165 --> 00:03:55.935 align:start size:94% position:6%
30% of Democrat-registered
non-Cuban Hispanics

00:03:55.935 --> 00:04:00.206
voted for Salazar 'cause we
do know that they promise

00:04:01.374 --> 00:04:04.644
paradise and what you
get is hell at the end.

00:04:04.644 --> 00:04:07.046
So anything that has
to do with socialism

00:04:07.046 --> 00:04:12.051
or socialist policies, you
may have some social programs

00:04:13.219 --> 00:04:14.754
that could benefit
the underprivileged,

00:04:14.754 --> 00:04:16.289
but don't give me socialism.

00:04:16.289 --> 00:04:19.058
And that's why Maria
Salazar is serving

00:04:19.058 --> 00:04:22.095
the most difficult district
in the state of Florida.

00:04:22.095 --> 00:04:27.066
Difficult meaning where you are
50/50, it's not that you are

00:04:27.066 --> 00:04:30.103 align:start size:97% position:3%
in a very highly concentrated
Republican district.

00:04:30.103 --> 00:04:31.371
No, no, no, no.

00:04:31.371 --> 00:04:33.706
This is, we're even,
one third Democrats,

00:04:33.706 --> 00:04:36.542
one third Republicans,
one third Independent.

00:04:36.542 --> 00:04:38.111
- Yeah, and that does
seem to be shifting

00:04:38.111 --> 00:04:39.045
though a little bit, right?

00:04:39.045 --> 00:04:40.313
Because after this last wave,

00:04:40.313 --> 00:04:42.548
I mean, DeSantis
took Miami, which-

00:04:42.548 --> 00:04:44.250
- Yes, Miami-Dade County.

00:04:44.250 --> 00:04:45.485
- Yeah.

00:04:45.485 --> 00:04:48.121
- First time in 20 years
a Republican governor.

00:04:48.121 --> 00:04:49.489
Why?

00:04:49.489 --> 00:04:52.392 align:start size:97% position:3%
Because we are understanding
that this country,

00:04:52.392 --> 00:04:56.262
politically speaking, is not
going the way we need it to.

00:04:56.262 --> 00:04:59.632 align:start size:97% position:3%
And what people have to
understand is that people say,

00:04:59.632 --> 00:05:01.801
"Well, because Florida
there was a red wave."

00:05:01.801 --> 00:05:05.071 align:start size:84% position:16%
Yeah, because you have
people in Florida,

00:05:05.071 --> 00:05:08.875 align:start size:97% position:3%
the people who live in Florida
come from either Venezuela

00:05:08.875 --> 00:05:11.377
or Cuba or Nicaragua
or Central America.

00:05:11.377 --> 00:05:12.211
Right?

00:05:12.211 --> 00:05:13.146
- Or worse, Los Angeles.

00:05:13.146 --> 00:05:15.515
- Well, okay, alright.

00:05:15.515 --> 00:05:17.817
So that, you have a
point of reference.

00:05:17.817 --> 00:05:18.885
- [Dave] Yeah.

00:05:18.885 --> 00:05:20.153 align:start size:88% position:13%
- You cannot
understand what's black

00:05:20.153 --> 00:05:22.388
if you have not seen
white or vice versa.

00:05:22.388 --> 00:05:24.957
So once my parents saw
black, really black.

00:05:24.957 --> 00:05:26.492
So now when they see white,

00:05:26.492 --> 00:05:28.795
they run away because they
have a point of reference.

00:05:28.795 --> 00:05:30.330
- [Dave] Yeah.

00:05:30.330 --> 00:05:32.398
But unfortunately some of the
members and some of the people

00:05:32.398 --> 00:05:35.068
that serve with me on the
House of Representatives,

00:05:35.068 --> 00:05:38.538
even though they may
have noble intentions,

00:05:38.538 --> 00:05:42.008 align:start size:97% position:3%
they are useful fools
'cause what they think that

00:05:42.008 --> 00:05:43.976
what they're pedaling
is good for others.

00:05:43.976 --> 00:05:47.347
No, they, because they have
never had the experience

00:05:47.347 --> 00:05:49.982
of being or living
in Cuba or Venezuela.

00:05:49.982 --> 00:05:51.384
Go for two weeks to Havana.

00:05:51.384 --> 00:05:52.852
(Dave laughing)

00:05:52.852 --> 00:05:54.721 align:start size:94% position:6%
I always tell them two
weeks only, make it a week

00:05:54.721 --> 00:05:57.523 align:start size:84% position:16%
with a Cuban family
living with no dollars

00:05:57.523 --> 00:06:00.093
and waiting to come
to the United States.

00:06:00.093 --> 00:06:01.728
Go live with them for one week.

00:06:01.728 --> 00:06:04.497
And then you tell me what
the beauties of socialism.

00:06:04.497 --> 00:06:06.799
Oh no, because we
don't really want

00:06:06.799 --> 00:06:10.370 align:start size:97% position:3%
the Cuban or the Venezuelan
type of socialism.

00:06:10.370 --> 00:06:12.472 align:start size:94% position:6%
Really, so what
socialism would you like?

00:06:12.472 --> 00:06:13.306
- Right.

00:06:13.306 --> 00:06:14.574
They want that one

00:06:14.574 --> 00:06:15.375
that's never been put
into practice somehow.

00:06:15.375 --> 00:06:16.642
- Or that we don't know.

00:06:16.642 --> 00:06:17.477
- Yeah.

00:06:17.477 --> 00:06:18.978
(Maria laughing)

00:06:18.978 --> 00:06:20.913
So how is it for you going
from your district in Miami,

00:06:20.913 --> 00:06:22.849 align:start size:97% position:3%
which is highly functional,
I mean, everything,

00:06:22.849 --> 00:06:25.284
I'm telling you, like,
I have no complaints.

00:06:25.284 --> 00:06:26.819
I wish that you're
my congresswoman.

00:06:26.819 --> 00:06:29.021
I wish I could come to you and
be like, fix a couple things.

00:06:29.021 --> 00:06:29.856
But it's working.

00:06:29.856 --> 00:06:30.857
Our roads are good.

00:06:30.857 --> 00:06:32.392
Our police are fantastic.

00:06:32.392 --> 00:06:33.526
It's clean, there's
no homeless people.

00:06:33.526 --> 00:06:35.061
- No riots.

00:06:35.061 --> 00:06:36.963
- There's no drugs on the
streets, there's no riots.

00:06:36.963 --> 00:06:39.899
But when you go from
that down in Florida

00:06:39.899 --> 00:06:42.068 align:start size:97% position:3%
and then you come here
where it's so dysfunctional

00:06:42.068 --> 00:06:43.603
and so crazy, and
just as you said,

00:06:43.603 --> 00:06:45.772
you're talking to members of
Congress who have, you know,

00:06:45.772 --> 00:06:47.440 align:start size:84% position:16%
their ideas
completely backwards.

00:06:47.440 --> 00:06:49.509
How do you put those
two things together?

00:06:51.010 --> 00:06:53.813
- You know, it's that we
speak another language.

00:06:53.813 --> 00:06:57.083
And I've been trying to,
I've been meaning to sit

00:06:57.083 --> 00:07:00.720 align:start size:97% position:3%
with some of the members that
like Democratic socialism

00:07:00.720 --> 00:07:02.054 align:start size:84% position:16%
and I've been
wanting to ask them

00:07:02.054 --> 00:07:03.956
what is it that you
know that I don't?

00:07:04.924 --> 00:07:05.758
I don't know.

00:07:05.758 --> 00:07:06.993
Tell me, explain to me,

00:07:06.993 --> 00:07:09.562
what is it that you
see that I don't see?

00:07:09.562 --> 00:07:12.565 align:start size:97% position:3%
Because Democrats and
Democratic socialists do not

00:07:12.565 --> 00:07:15.334
have a monopoly on compassion.

00:07:15.334 --> 00:07:17.069
We are compassionate too.

00:07:17.937 --> 00:07:19.439
I wanna help those who are,

00:07:19.439 --> 00:07:22.108
I wanna help the Browns
and the African Americans

00:07:22.108 --> 00:07:24.544 align:start size:94% position:6%
and those kids that
don't have good schooling

00:07:24.544 --> 00:07:27.780
because I know that education
is the way out of poverty.

00:07:27.780 --> 00:07:29.015
I wanna help them too.

00:07:29.015 --> 00:07:31.884
But I don't want to, I
don't want atrophy them

00:07:31.884 --> 00:07:34.220 align:start size:84% position:16%
